      barrier: { zh: "方法只能给下界且依赖标志词；更深的难题是当训练语料本身已被 AI 污染，“人类基线”再也无法从新数据里干净地取样。", en: "The method yields only a lower bound and leans on marker words. The deeper trouble is that once the corpus itself is AI-contaminated, a clean 'human baseline' can no longer be sampled from new data at all." },
      subQuestions: [
        { zh: "当模型刻意避开已公开的标志词，超额词频的下界会掉到什么水平，还剩多少可检测信号？", en: "If models deliberately avoid the published marker words, how far does the excess-vocabulary lower bound fall, and how much detectable signal survives?" },
        { zh: "除词频外，句法与篇章结构上是否存在更难规避的指纹？它们的下界估计与词频法一致吗？", en: "Beyond word frequency, are there syntactic or discourse-level fingerprints that are harder to evade — and do their lower bounds agree with the lexical estimate?" },
        { zh: "人类作者读多了 AI 文本后自发同质化的部分，能否与直接代写在同一估计框架里分开？", en: "Can the homogenization human authors adopt after reading a lot of AI text be separated, inside the same estimation framework, from text written by the machine outright?" },
      ],
