    slug: "geographic-sampling-debt-biodiversity-science",
    title: { zh: "生物多样性的地域采样债务", en: "Geographic Sampling Debt in Biodiversity Science" },
    qfocus: { zh: "一张生物多样性热点图上，多少信号来自物种本身，多少只来自道路、经费与采集史？", en: "On a biodiversity hotspot map, how much of the signal comes from the species themselves and how much from roads, funding and collecting history?" },
    domain: "交叉",
    cluster: { code: "C34", zh: "无知测绘·盲区科学", en: "Mapping ignorance & blind spots" },
    scores: [5, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 3, 3, 5],
    citation: {
      url: "https://doi.org/10.1093/biosci/biac116",
      title: "Measuring What We Don't Know: Biodiversity Catalogs Reveal Bias in Taxonomic Effort",
      venue: "BioScience",
      year: 2023,
    },
    brief: { zh: "把出现记录密度按可达性、类群投入与数字化史分解，用协变量潜在相互作用模型补上被共同缺测的物种与互作，再用新采的野外样本而非同一档案做外部检验。", en: "Decompose occurrence-record density into accessibility, taxonomic effort and digitization history, use covariate-informed latent interaction models to fill in jointly under-sampled species and interactions, then validate against freshly collected field samples rather than the same archive." },
    literature: [
      { title: "Covariate-Informed Latent Interaction Models: Addressing Geographic & Taxonomic Bias in Predicting Bird–Plant Interactions", venue: "Journal of the American Statistical Association", year: 2023, url: "https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.2023.2208390" },
      { title: "A large‐scale assessment of ant diversity across the Brazilian Amazon Basin: integrating geographic, ecological and morphological drivers of sampling bias", venue: "Ecography", year: 2022, url: "https://doi.org/10.1111/ecog.06295" },
    ],
    depth: {
      overview: { zh: "采样债务问的不是还有多少物种没被发现，而是已收集的数据如何把采样努力误读成自然格局。《Ecography》在巴西亚马逊的大尺度蚂蚁调查中拆解了道路可达性、环境与形态驱动的偏差；《BioScience》用生物多样性目录量出类群研究投入的严重不均。", en: "Sampling debt is not about how many species remain undiscovered; it is about how already-collected data misread sampling effort as a pattern of nature. Ecography decomposed accessibility, environmental and morphological drivers of bias in a large-scale ant survey across the Brazilian Amazon; BioScience used biodiversity catalogs to quantify how unevenly taxonomic effort is spread." },
      whyMatters: { zh: "保护优先区大多画在这些记录之上，若热点其实是公路热点，资源就会持续投向已被研究透的地方；但偏差校正模型再精巧，也无法凭空恢复从未被观察的物种与相互作用。", en: "Conservation priority maps are drawn on top of these records, so if the hotspots are really road hotspots, resources keep flowing to places already well studied. And however refined the bias-correction model, it cannot recover species and interactions that were never observed." },
      ifAnswered: { zh: "优先地图可以把数据债务与灭绝风险分层显示，让我们不知道那里有什么本身成为投入依据，而不是被当成那里没有。", en: "Priority maps could show data debt and extinction risk as separate layers, so that 'we do not know what is there' becomes a reason to invest rather than being read as 'nothing is there'." },
      approaches: [
        { zh: "以道路距离、经费与数字化史为协变量，建模出现记录密度中的努力成分。", en: "Model the effort component of occurrence-record density using road distance, funding and digitization history as covariates." },
        { zh: "用协变量潜在相互作用模型预测鸟—植物网络中地理与分类共同缺测的连边。", en: "Predict the jointly geographically and taxonomically missing links in bird–plant networks with covariate-informed latent interaction models." },
        { zh: "清洗 GBIF 与馆藏数据的重复记录、坐标误差与分类异名，并报告时间漂移。", en: "Clean duplicate records, coordinate errors and taxonomic synonymy from GBIF and museum data, and report the temporal drift that remains." },
      ],
      barrier: { zh: "校正模型只能在同一批有偏档案里交叉验证，而检验它是否真的还原了自然格局，需要去从未被采过的地方重新采样——那恰恰是采样债务最重的地方。", en: "Correction models can only be cross-validated inside the same biased archive, while testing whether they truly recover the natural pattern requires new sampling exactly where nobody has ever sampled — which is precisely where the debt is deepest." },
      subQuestions: [
        { zh: "在同一区域新采的野外样本上，偏差校正模型的预测误差比未校正低多少？", en: "On freshly collected field samples from the same region, how much lower is the prediction error of a bias-corrected model than an uncorrected one?" },
        { zh: "类群研究投入的不均，能否与地域可达性偏差在统计上被分离开？", en: "Can unevenness in taxonomic effort be statistically separated from geographic accessibility bias?" },
        { zh: "一张把数据债务与灭绝风险分层的优先图，会把保护资源重新分配到哪里？", en: "Where would a priority map that layers data debt separately from extinction risk redirect conservation resources?" },
      ],
    },
