      barrier: { zh: "rubric 判分本身多半也由 LLM 执行，AI 判 AI 的循环性未解；而 ResearchClawBench 上最强的 Claude Code 均分仅 21.5，再发现远谈不上可靠。", en: "Rubric scoring is itself mostly carried out by LLMs, leaving the circularity of AI judging AI unresolved; and on ResearchClawBench the strongest entrant, Claude Code, averaged only 21.5 — re-discovery is nowhere near reliable." },
      subQuestions: [
        { zh: "隐藏了方法之后，任务包里残留的数据组织方式是否仍在泄漏原论文的思路？", en: "Once the method is hidden, does the way data are organized in the task package still leak the original paper's line of thought?" },
        { zh: "禁网检索能挡住外部泄漏，但参数里的记忆该如何在评测中被单独测量？", en: "A no-retrieval protocol blocks external leakage, but how is memorization held in the parameters measured separately during evaluation?" },
        { zh: "任务库滚动更新时，如何保证新旧批次的难度可比，而不是逐年变松？", en: "As the task pool rolls forward, how is difficulty kept comparable between batches rather than drifting easier year over year?" },
      ],
